<PageTitle>Blazor AI Prompt Component — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="AI prompt" Category="Components" ControlName="AIPromptControl · AppBarControl · ToolbarControl"
                   Tagline="A prompt box with suggestions, command buttons, a response card and a history; your application supplies the model."
                   SourcePath="AIPromptControl.razor; AIPromptModels.cs; LlmResultCard.razor; AppBarControl.razor; ToolbarControl.razor; ToolbarButtonControl.razor; ToolbarSeparatorControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>AIPromptControl</code> is the screen side of a text-generation feature: a multi-line prompt, suggestion buttons that fill it, a Generate
            button, one button per <code>AIPromptCommand</code>, and an <code>LlmResultCard</code> that shows the response with a button to use it. The
            control calls no service. You pass a <code>Generate</code> delegate that receives an <code>AIPromptRequest</code> (the prompt, and the command
            if one was clicked) with a <code>CancellationToken</code> and returns the response text; the control handles the busy state, cancelling, the
            error message and a history of responses. Both examples on this page pass a stub that returns canned text.
        </p>
        <p>
            The second example puts it on a desk screen: an <code>AppBarControl</code> for the title row, a <code>ToolbarControl</code> of
            <code>ToolbarButtonControl</code>s and <code>ToolbarSeparatorControl</code>s for the commands, and the prompt in a side panel.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="prompt" Title="Prompt, suggestions and commands" RazorCode="@Code.Prompt" CSharpCode="@Code.PromptCs" CssCode="@Code.PromptCss">
            <Description>
                <p>
                    A suggestion only fills the prompt; Generate sends it. Shorten, Expand and Friendlier tone send the same prompt with their
                    <code>AIPromptCommand</code>, and the card's badge names the command. Use in draft raises <code>Apply</code> with the response on show,
                    and the page copies its <code>Output</code> into the draft below. From the second response on, a row of history buttons brings back an
                    earlier one; Dismiss hides the card and keeps the response in the history. The count under the control comes from <code>Generated</code>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    No model is called. <code>Generate</code> is a page method, <code>StubGenerateAsync</code>, that waits 1.2 seconds on the request's token
                    (so Cancel stops it), picks canned text by a word in the prompt and switches on the command's <code>Key</code>. It ignores
                    <code>Instruction</code>, which a real provider would add to the prompt. An application connects its own provider through the same delegate.
                </p>
            </Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="ai">
                    <AIPromptControl @bind-Prompt="_prompt" Suggestions="_suggestions" Commands="_commands" Generate="StubGenerateAsync"
                                     Rows="3" Placeholder="Ask about a trip request…" ApplyLabel="Use in draft"
                                     Apply="r => _draft = r.Output" Generated="r => _responses++" />
                    <p class="ai-note">Responses so far: @_responses</p>
                    <div class="ai-label">Draft for the traveller</div>
                    <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_draft" Multiline="true" Rows="5" Width="100%" aria-label="Draft for the traveller"
                                    Placeholder="Use in draft puts the response here; edit it as you like." />
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="app-bar" Title="From an app bar and toolbar" RazorCode="@Code.AppBar" CSharpCode="@Code.AppBarCs" CssCode="@Code.AppBarCss">
            <Description>
                <p>
                    <code>AppBarControl</code> lays out its three slots in a header: an icon and the title, a subtitle, and a badge that follows the save state.
                    Under it, a <code>ToolbarControl</code> holds <code>ToolbarButtonControl</code>s with Bootstrap icon classes in <code>IconCss</code> and
                    captions in <code>Label</code>, with <code>ToolbarSeparatorControl</code>s between the groups. The buttons only report themselves in the
                    status line; nothing is exported or printed. Save is <code>Disabled</code> until a new request, an edit to the notes or an added response.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Export has <code>HasDropdown</code>, which draws the arrow and nothing else, so the page opens its own two-item panel under it; a pick,
                    Export again or any other toolbar button closes it. AI assistant is a toggle through <code>Selected</code> and shows the prompt in a side
                    panel (hidden, not removed, so its history survives); its Add to notes appends the response to the notes. The Captions checkbox is the
                    toolbar's own (<code>ShowCaptionsToggle</code>), bound here through <code>ShowCaptions</code> and <code>ShowCaptionsChanged</code>; the
                    switch above sets <code>Vertical</code> on every button. The library styles <code>Selected</code> only on <code>Large</code> buttons, so
                    the page adds the pressed tint (CSS tab).
                </p>
            </Description>
            <Controls>
                <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_vertical" Label="Vertical buttons" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="qd">
                    <AppBarControl>
                        <StartContent><SvgIconControl Name="document" Size="20px" /><strong>Quote desk</strong></StartContent>
                        <ChildContent><span class="qd-sub">Lisbon desk · requests from the web form</span></ChildContent>
                        <EndContent><BadgeControl Text="@(_dirty ? "Unsaved" : "Saved")" Variant="@(_dirty ? BadgeVariant.Warning : BadgeVariant.Success)" /></EndContent>
                    </AppBarControl>
                    <ToolbarControl ShowCaptions="_captions" ShowCaptionsChanged="SetCaptions">
                        <ToolbarButtonControl Label="New request" IconCss="bi bi-file-earmark-plus" Vertical="_vertical" OnClick="NewRequest" />
                        <ToolbarButtonControl Label="Save" IconCss="bi bi-save" Vertical="_vertical" Disabled="!_dirty" OnClick="Save" />
                        <ToolbarSeparatorControl />
                        <span class="qd-export">
                            <ToolbarButtonControl Label="Export" IconCss="bi bi-box-arrow-up" Vertical="_vertical" HasDropdown="true"
                                                  OnClick="() => _exportOpen = !_exportOpen" />
                            @if (_exportOpen)
                            {
                                <div class="qd-menu">
                                    <ButtonControl CssClass="qd-menu-item" OnClick='() => Act("Export › PDF quote")'>PDF quote</ButtonControl>
                                    <ButtonControl CssClass="qd-menu-item" OnClick='() => Act("Export › CSV itinerary")'>CSV itinerary</ButtonControl>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </span>
                        <ToolbarButtonControl Label="Print" IconCss="bi bi-printer" Vertical="_vertical" OnClick='() => Act("Print")' />
                        <ToolbarSeparatorControl />
                        <ToolbarButtonControl Label="AI assistant" IconCss="bi bi-stars" Vertical="_vertical" Selected="_assistant" OnClick="ToggleAssistant" />
                    </ToolbarControl>
                    <p class="qd-status" role="status">Last action: @_last</p>
                    <div class="qd-body">
                        <div class="qd-notes">
                            <div class="qd-label">Agent notes, request QD-@(_request)</div>
                            <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_notes" @bind-Value:after="MarkDirty" Multiline="true" Rows="8" Width="100%" aria-label="Agent notes" />
                        </div>
                        <aside class="qd-panel" hidden="@(!_assistant)" aria-label="AI assistant">
                            <AIPromptControl @bind-Prompt="_deskPrompt" Suggestions="_suggestions" Commands="_commands" Generate="StubGenerateAsync"
                                             Rows="3" ApplyLabel="Add to notes" Apply="AddToNotes" />
                        </aside>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-aipromptcontrol-parameters" Title="AIPromptControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Prompt.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="AIPromptControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Prompt" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-aipromptcontrol-events" Title="AIPromptControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.PromptEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="AIPromptControl events" Rows="Vocab.PromptEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-aipromptcontrol-methods" Title="AIPromptControl methods and read-only properties" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.PromptMethods.Length, "members")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="AIPromptControl methods and read-only properties" Rows="Vocab.PromptMethods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-aipromptmodels" Title="Request, command and result" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Request.Length + Vocab.Command.Length + Vocab.Result.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AIPromptRequest" Rows="Vocab.Request" />
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AIPromptCommand" Rows="Vocab.Command" />
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AIPromptResult" Rows="Vocab.Result" />
                <p>All three are sealed positional records in <code>Fx.ControlKit.AI</code>, so they compare by value and are built with <code>new(…)</code>.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-llmresultcard-parameters" Title="LlmResultCard parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Card.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="LlmResultCard parameters" Rows="Vocab.Card" />
                <p>
                    <code>AIPromptControl</code> sets <code>OutputText</code>, <code>OriginalText</code>, <code>OperationLabel</code>, <code>IsBusy</code>,
                    <code>ErrorMessage</code>, <code>OnApply</code>, <code>OnDismiss</code> and <code>ApplyLabel</code>; the other parameters are for hosts that
                    place the card (namespace <code>Fx.ControlKit.Editor</code>) themselves. While an error is shown there is no response, so the card has no
                    Dismiss button; the next request clears the error.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <code>ResultAction</code> is <code>(string Label, EventCallback OnClick, bool IsPrimary = false, bool Disabled = false, string? Title = null,
                    string? IconSvg = null)</code>: <code>IsPrimary</code> picks the filled style, <code>Title</code> the tooltip, and <code>IconSvg</code> is
                    inserted before the label as raw markup, so pass only markup you trust. <code>Variant</code> is <code>(string Label, string Text)</code>.
                    Both records are nested in <code>LlmResultCard</code>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The header's copy button copies the text selected inside the card, or else the whole response, as plain text. It calls
                    <code>fxClipboard.copyFromCard</code> from the library's <code>editor-control.js</code>, which only <code>EditorControl</code> and
                    <code>EditorLiteControl</code> import; on a page with neither editor the call fails silently and nothing is copied.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The stylesheet reads <code>--panel</code>, <code>--panel-2</code>, <code>--border</code>, <code>--ink</code>, <code>--muted</code>,
                    <code>--accent</code>, <code>--accent-strong</code> and <code>--accent-2</code>, with warm built-in fallbacks; both examples set them on
                    their wrapper (CSS tabs). The response body's background (<code>#fef7ef</code>), the error box and the echo banner have fixed colours; the
                    examples override the body's by class.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-appbarcontrol-parameters" Title="AppBarControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.AppBar.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="AppBarControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.AppBar" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-appbarposition" Title="AppBarPosition" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Position.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="AppBarPosition" Rows="Vocab.Position" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-toolbarcontrol-parameters" Title="ToolbarControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Toolbar.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ToolbarControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Toolbar" />
                <p>
                    With captions off the root gets <code>fx-toolbar--no-captions</code>: <code>Label</code> captions are hidden, buttons shrink to 30px high,
                    and every <code>ToolbarButtonControl</code> shows its tooltip even with <code>ShowTooltip</code> false. Text passed as a button's
                    <code>ChildContent</code> stays visible. For <code>CssClass</code> the stylesheet also defines <code>fx-toolbar--wrap</code> (the toolbar
                    itself wraps), <code>fx-toolbar--scroll</code> (horizontal scrolling) and <code>fx-toolbar--large-tools</code> (white, unbordered, at least
                    128px high, for <code>Large</code> buttons).
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-toolbarbuttoncontrol-parameters" Title="ToolbarButtonControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Button.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ToolbarButtonControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Button" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-toolbarseparatorcontrol-parameters" Title="ToolbarSeparatorControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Separator.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ToolbarSeparatorControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Separator" />
                <p>A 1px line, 28px high (22px with captions off), with 4px either side.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li><code>AIPromptControl</code> renders a <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> named by <code>AriaLabel</code>, and the prompt's text area carries the same <code>aria-label</code>; the placeholder is not its name.</li>
            <li>Every action is a native button. Tab moves from the prompt through the suggestions to Generate, the commands and, while a request runs, Cancel. The inner toolbar has <code>role="toolbar"</code> but no arrow-key handling, so each button is its own Tab stop; the same is true of <code>ToolbarControl</code> used on its own.</li>
            <li>Progress and results are not announced: the "Generating…" row and the response card have no live region. The only <code>role="status"</code> in the control is the message shown while <code>Generate</code> is null. The second example's status line is the page's own <code>role="status"</code>.</li>
            <li>The history row's <code>aria-label="Response history"</code> sits on a plain <code>div</code> with no role, and each history button's pressed state is passed as a C# <code>bool</code>, which Blazor writes as an empty attribute on the current button and omits on the others, so no pressed state is exposed.</li>
            <li>In the card, the copy and × buttons are named by their <code>title</code>; Original text is a native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>. Variant tabs have <code>role="tab"</code> and <code>aria-selected</code> but no arrow keys (<code>AIPromptControl</code> does not use them).</li>
            <li><code>ToolbarButtonControl</code> sets <code>aria-label</code> from <code>Title</code>, else <code>Label</code>, else <code>IconAlt</code>, so the name survives hidden captions; an <code>IconCss</code> icon is <code>aria-hidden</code>. <code>Selected</code> writes <code>aria-pressed="true"</code> and leaves the attribute out when false, so a toggle that is off reads as a plain button. <code>HasDropdown</code> adds no <code>aria-haspopup</code> or <code>aria-expanded</code>, and the control accepts no extra attributes to add them. Keyboard focus shows a dotted outline.</li>
            <li><code>ToolbarSeparatorControl</code> is <code>role="separator"</code> with <code>aria-orientation="vertical"</code>. <code>ToolbarControl</code> accepts no <code>aria-label</code>, so two toolbars on one screen cannot be told apart by name; its Captions checkbox is a native checkbox inside its label.</li>
            <li><code>AppBarControl</code> is a <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> (a banner landmark only when it is not inside <code>main</code>, <code>article</code>, <code>aside</code>, <code>nav</code> or <code>section</code>) wrapping a <code>ToolbarControl</code>, so its title and end items sit inside a <code>role="toolbar"</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>A button that opens its own panel, and plain buttons: <a href="demo/buttons#dropdown">Buttons</a>.</li>
            <li>A pressed-state button outside a toolbar: <a href="demo/toggle-buttons">Toggle buttons</a>.</li>
            <li>A default action with its alternatives in a real menu: <a href="demo/split-button">Split button</a>.</li>
            <li><code>EditorControl</code>'s built-in toolbar (<code>ShowToolbar</code>) is a <code>ToolbarControl</code>: <a href="demo/rich-text-editor">Rich text editor</a>.</li>
            <li><code>ChatControl</code>, <code>InlineAIPromptControl</code>, <code>PromptBoxControl</code>, <code>SmartPasteButtonControl</code> and <code>SpeechToTextButtonControl</code> are separate controls in <code>Fx.ControlKit.AI</code>, not covered here.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

@code {
    // Prompt
    private string _prompt = "Draft a three-day Lisbon itinerary for two";
    private string _draft = "";
    private int _responses;
    private readonly string[] _suggestions =
    {
        "Draft a three-day Lisbon itinerary for two",
        "Summarise this trip request for the agent",
        "Write a polite reply declining the dates",
    };
    private readonly AIPromptCommand[] _commands =
    {
        new("shorten", "Shorten", "Reduce the answer to one sentence."),
        new("expand", "Expand", "Add one practical detail."),
        new("friendlier", "Friendlier tone", "Use a warmer, more personal tone."),
    };

    // Stub provider: no model is called. An application passes its own provider to Generate.
    private static readonly TravelData.Package Lisbon = TravelData.Packages.First(p => p.City == "Lisbon");
    private static readonly string[] Itinerary =
    {
        "Day 1: arrive, check in near the old town and walk up to a viewpoint for sunset.",
        "Day 2: tram through the old town in the morning, the riverside at Belém in the afternoon.",
        "Day 3: day trip to Sintra, back in Lisbon for a farewell dinner.",
        "Tip: book the Sintra tickets a day ahead.",
    };
    private static readonly string[] Summary =
    {
        "Lisbon, 12–15 May, two adults.",
        "Wants a hotel within walking distance of the old town, and one day trip.",
        "Open question: are the dates flexible? The form leaves it blank.",
        $"Closest package: {Lisbon.Name} ({Lisbon.Nights} nights), shortened to three.",
    };
    private static readonly string[] Decline =
    {
        "Thank you for your request for Lisbon on 12–15 May.",
        "We cannot confirm those dates: the hotels we work with are fully booked that week.",
        "We can offer the same trip from 19 May, or another hotel on your dates.",
        "If you reply by Friday, we will hold the 19 May option for you.",
    };
    private static async Task<string> StubGenerateAsync(AIPromptRequest request, CancellationToken token)
    {
        await Task.Delay(1200, token);   // Cancel stops the wait
        var prompt = request.Prompt.ToLowerInvariant();
        var lines = prompt.Contains("itinerary") ? Itinerary
            : prompt.Contains("summar") ? Summary
            : prompt.Contains("declin") ? Decline
            : null;
        if (lines is null)
            return $"(Stub) No canned answer for \"{request.Prompt}\". Try a suggestion; an application would send the prompt to its own provider.";
        var body = string.Join("\n", lines[..3]);
        return request.Command?.Key switch
        {
            "shorten" => lines[0],
            "expand" => body + "\n" + lines[3],
            "friendlier" => "Hello, and thank you for thinking of us!\n" + body + "\nWe would love to help you plan this.",
            _ => body,
        };
    }

    // App bar (the side panel reuses _suggestions, _commands and StubGenerateAsync from the first example)
    private bool _captions = true, _vertical, _exportOpen, _assistant = true, _dirty;
    private int _request = 1042;
    private string _last = "none yet";
    private string _deskPrompt = "Summarise this trip request for the agent";
    private string _notes = "Phoned on Monday: two adults, 12–15 May, hotel within walking distance of the old town.";
    private void Act(string action)
    {
        _exportOpen = false;
        _last = action;
    }
    private void NewRequest()
    {
        Act("New request");
        _request++;
        _notes = "";
        _dirty = true;
    }
    private void Save()
    {
        Act("Save");
        _dirty = false;
    }
    private void ToggleAssistant()
    {
        _assistant = !_assistant;
        Act(_assistant ? "AI assistant on" : "AI assistant off");
    }
    private void SetCaptions(bool on)
    {
        _captions = on;
        Act(on ? "Captions on" : "Captions off");
    }
    private void MarkDirty() => _dirty = true;
    private void AddToNotes(AIPromptResult result)
    {
        _notes = _notes.Length > 0 ? _notes + "\n\n" + result.Output : result.Output;
        _dirty = true;
        Act("Add to notes, from the AI assistant");
    }

    // Vocabulary rows, one per public member (FlexCore 0.2.49). Base-class parameters marked (base).
    private static class Vocab
    {
        public static readonly ApiRow[] Prompt =
        {
            new("Prompt", "The prompt, in a multi-line <code>TextBoxControl</code> that updates on every keystroke; a suggestion click replaces it. The control writes its own copy, so bind it with <code>@bind-Prompt</code>; otherwise the parent's value can replace the typed text when the parent re-renders.", "string", "\"\""),
            new("Generate", "Your provider. Called with an <code>AIPromptRequest</code> and a token that Cancel and disposal cancel; returns the response text. While it is null the Generate and command buttons stay disabled and a status line asks for a provider.", "Func&lt;AIPromptRequest, CancellationToken, Task&lt;string&gt;&gt;?", "null"),
            new("Suggestions", "One button per string under the prompt. A click replaces the prompt and raises <code>PromptChanged</code>; it does not generate.", "IReadOnlyList&lt;string&gt;", "Array.Empty&lt;string&gt;()"),
            new("Commands", "One button per command after Generate, captioned with its <code>Text</code>. A click generates with the command in the request, and the card's badge shows its <code>Text</code>.", "IReadOnlyList&lt;AIPromptCommand&gt;", "Array.Empty&lt;AIPromptCommand&gt;()"),
            new("MaxHistory", "Most responses kept in <code>History</code>, newest first. Below 1 keeps one.", "int", "10"),
            new("Rows", "Height of the prompt box in lines.", "int", "4"),
            new("AriaLabel", "<code>aria-label</code> of the section and of the prompt box.", "string", "\"AI prompt\""),
            new("Placeholder", "Placeholder of the prompt box.", "string", "\"Enter a prompt…\""),
            new("ApplyLabel", "Caption of the card's apply button. The button is drawn whether or not <code>Apply</code> has a handler.", "string", "\"Use response\""),
            new("FooterContent", "Rendered last inside the section, after the history row.", "RenderFragment?", "null"),
            new("Enabled (base)", "False disables the prompt box, the suggestions, Generate and the commands, and makes the apply button do nothing. The history buttons and Dismiss still work.", "bool", "true"),
            new("Visible (base)", "False adds <code>display:none</code> to the section.", "bool", "true"),
            new("Id / CssClass / Style (base)", "On the <code>section.fx-ai-prompt</code>.", "string?", "null"),
            new("(unmatched attributes)", "Written on the section after its own attributes, so a <code>class</code> or <code>aria-label</code> given here replaces the control's own.", "Dictionary&lt;string,object&gt;"),
        };
        public static readonly ApiRow[] PromptEvents =
        {
            new("PromptChanged", "After every keystroke in the prompt box and after a suggestion click.", "string"),
            new("Generated", "After a response has arrived and joined the front of <code>History</code> as the response on show. Not raised for a cancelled or failed request.", "AIPromptResult"),
            new("Apply", "When the card's apply button is clicked, with the response on show: the newest, or the one picked in the history row. Ignored while busy or disabled.", "AIPromptResult"),
        };
        public static readonly ApiRow[] PromptMethods =
        {
            new("GenerateAsync(AIPromptCommand? command = null)", "What Generate (no command) and the command buttons call. Does nothing unless the control is enabled and idle, <code>Generate</code> is set and the prompt is not blank. Otherwise hides the current response, sets <code>IsBusy</code>, awaits <code>Generate</code>, and on success puts the result at the front of <code>History</code>, shows it and raises <code>Generated</code>. Any exception other than the cancellation sets <code>ErrorMessage</code> to its <code>Message</code>.", "Task"),
            new("CancelAsync()", "Cancels the running request's token and clears <code>IsBusy</code> at once. A response that still arrives afterwards is dropped.", "Task"),
            new("Dispose()", "Cancels a running request.", "void"),
            new("IsBusy", "Read-only. True from the start of a request until it finishes or is cancelled.", "bool"),
            new("ErrorMessage", "Read-only. The last failure's message, or null; cleared when the next request starts.", "string?"),
            new("History", "Read-only. The responses, newest first, at most <code>MaxHistory</code>.", "IReadOnlyList&lt;AIPromptResult&gt;"),
        };
        public static readonly ApiRow[] Request =
        {
            new("Prompt", "The prompt as it was when the request started.", "string"),
            new("Command", "The command that was clicked, or null for Generate.", "AIPromptCommand?"),
        };
        public static readonly ApiRow[] Command =
        {
            new("Key", "Your identifier, passed through in the request; the control does not read it.", "string"),
            new("Text", "Button caption; also the result's <code>Command</code> and the card's badge.", "string"),
